  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The statistical methodology outlined above for half sibs also applies to full-sib analysis, provided the interpretations of the within- and among-family components of variance are modified appropriately. For the special case in which there are no dominance effects and no common environmental effects, twice the intra-class correlation coefficient for full sibs provides an estimate of the narrow-sense heritability. However, since the significance of these two sources of variance is generally unknown in advance of a quantitative-genetic analysis, it is best to avoid the exclusive use of full sibs to estimate $ h^{2} $.",
      "source_page": 584,
      "printed_page": 564,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p018:b5",
        "Genetics_chapter18:p018:b6"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        143.0,
        1102.0,
        1104.0,
        1371.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        584
      ],
