      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "e400d14e1788a7f426314eec17aeef7865316272e56a8f898e3b2b4144be33ab"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "On the other hand, a supplementary full-sib analysis can be valuable precisely because it provides information on the relative significance of the components of variance associated with dominance and common environmental effects. Such an analysis is only a small step beyond the paternal half-sib design. As before, N randomly selected fathers (sires) are each mated to several different females (dams), but now several (rather than one) offspring are assayed",
      "source_page": 584,
      "printed_page": 564,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p018:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
