    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "An obvious problem with the preceding set of equations is that they are overdetermined — there are seven causal sources of variance, but only three observable variance components. The usual approach in sib analysis is to assume that the epistatic sources of variance are of negligible significance, so that",
